<section>
  <exercises>
    <heading level="1">5.4 Section Exercises</heading>
    <heading level="1">Verbal</heading>
    <exercise number="1" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>If division of a polynomial by a binomial results in a remainder of zero, what can be conclude?</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>The binomial is a factor of the polynomial.</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="2" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>If a polynomial of degree $$n$$ is divided by a binomial of degree 1, what is the degree of the quotient?</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <heading level="1">Algebraic</heading>
    <paragraph>For the following exercises, use long division to divide. Specify the quotient and the remainder.</paragraph>
    <exercise number="3" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\left( {x^{2} + 5x - 1} \right) \div \left( {x - 1} \right)$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$x+6+ 5 x-1 ,quotient:x+6,remainder:5 x+6+ 5 x-1 ,quotient:x+6,remainder:5$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="4" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\left( {2x^{2} - 9x - 5} \right) \div \left( {x - 5} \right)$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="5" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\left( {3x^{2} + 23x + 14} \right) \div \left( {x + 7} \right)$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$3x+2,quotient: 3x+2,remainder: 0 3x+2,quotient: 3x+2,remainder: 0$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="6" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\left( {4x^{2} - 10x + 6} \right) \div \left( {4x + 2} \right)$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="7" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\left( {6x^{2} - 25x - 25} \right) \div \left( {6x + 5} \right)$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$x-5,quotient:x-5,remainder:0 x-5,quotient:x-5,remainder:0$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="8" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\left( {- x^{2} - 1} \right) \div \left( {x + 1} \right)$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="9" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\left( {2x^{2} - 3x + 2} \right) \div \left( {x + 2} \right)$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$2x-7+ 16 x+2 ,quotient:2x-7,remainder:16 2x-7+ 16 x+2 ,quotient:2x-7,remainder:16$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="10" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\left( {x^{3} - 126} \right) \div \left( {x - 5} \right)$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="11" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\left( {3x^{2} - 5x + 4} \right) \div \left( {3x + 1} \right)$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$x-2+ 6 3x+1 ,quotient:x-2,remainder:6 x-2+ 6 3x+1 ,quotient:x-2,remainder:6$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="12" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\left( {x^{3} - 3x^{2} + 5x - 6} \right) \div \left( {x - 2} \right)$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="13" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\left( {2x^{3} + 3x^{2} - 4x + 15} \right) \div \left( {x + 3} \right)$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$2 x 2 -3x+5,quotient:2 x 2 -3x+5,remainder:0 2 x 2 -3x+5,quotient:2 x 2 -3x+5,remainder:0$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <paragraph>For the following exercises, use synthetic division to find the quotient. Ensure the equation is in the form required by synthetic division. (Hint: divide the dividend and divisor by the coefficient of the linear term in the divisor.)</paragraph>
    <exercise number="14" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\left( {3x^{3} + 2x^{2} - x + 4} \right) \div \left( {x - 3} \right)$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="15" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\left( {2x^{3} - 6x^{2} - 7x + 6} \right) \div (x - 4)$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$2 x 2 +2x+1+ 10 x-4 2 x 2 +2x+1+ 10 x-4$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="16" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\left( {6x^{3} - 10x^{2} - 7x - 15} \right) \div (x + 1)$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="17" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\left( {4x^{3} - 12x^{2} - 5x - 1} \right) \div (2x + 1)$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$2 x 2 -7x+1- 2 2x+1 2 x 2 -7x+1- 2 2x+1$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="18" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\left( {9x^{3} - 9x^{2} + 18x + 5} \right) \div (3x - 1)$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="19" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\left( {3x^{3} - 2x^{2} + x - 4} \right) \div \left( {x + 3} \right)$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$3 x 2 -11x+34- 106 x+3 3 x 2 -11x+34- 106 x+3$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="20" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\left( {- 6x^{3} + x^{2} - 4} \right) \div \left( {2x - 3} \right)$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="21" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\left( {2x^{3} + 7x^{2} - 13x - 3} \right) \div \left( {2x - 3} \right)$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$x 2 +5x+1 x 2 +5x+1$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="22" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\left( {3x^{3} - 5x^{2} + 2x + 3} \right) \div (x + 2)$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="23" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\left( {4x^{3} - 5x^{2} + 13} \right) \div (x + 4)$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$4 x 2 -21x+84- 323 x+4 4 x 2 -21x+84- 323 x+4$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="24" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\left( {x^{3} - 3x + 2} \right) \div \left( {x + 2} \right)$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="25" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\left( {x^{3} - 21x^{2} + 147x - 343} \right) \div \left( {x - 7} \right)$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$x 2 -14x+49 x 2 -14x+49$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="26" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\left( {x^{3} - 15x^{2} + 75x - 125} \right) \div \left( {x - 5} \right)$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="27" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\left( {9x^{3} - x + 2} \right) \div \left( {3x - 1} \right)$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$3 x 2 +x+ 2 3x-1 3 x 2 +x+ 2 3x-1$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="28" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\left( {6x^{3} - x^{2} + 5x + 2} \right) \div \left( {3x + 1} \right)$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="29" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\left( {x^{4} + x^{3} - 3x^{2} - 2x + 1} \right) \div \left( {x + 1} \right)$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$x 3 -3x+1 x 3 -3x+1$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="30" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\left( {x^{4} - 3x^{2} + 1} \right) \div \left( {x - 1} \right)$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="31" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\left( {x^{4} + 2x^{3} - 3x^{2} + 2x + 6} \right) \div \left( {x + 3} \right)$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$x 3 - x 2 +2 x 3 - x 2 +2$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="32" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\left( {x^{4} - 10x^{3} + 37x^{2} - 60x + 36} \right) \div \left( {x - 2} \right)$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="33" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\left( {x^{4} - 8x^{3} + 24x^{2} - 32x + 16} \right) \div \left( {x - 2} \right)$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$x 3 -6 x 2 +12x-8 x 3 -6 x 2 +12x-8$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="34" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\left( {x^{4} + 5x^{3} - 3x^{2} - 13x + 10} \right) \div \left( {x + 5} \right)$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="35" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\left( {x^{4} - 12x^{3} + 54x^{2} - 108x + 81} \right) \div \left( {x - 3} \right)$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$x 3 -9 x 2 +27x-27 x 3 -9 x 2 +27x-27$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="36" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\left( {4x^{4} - 2x^{3} - 4x + 2} \right) \div \left( {2x - 1} \right)$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="37" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\left( {4x^{4} + 2x^{3} - 4x^{2} + 2x + 2} \right) \div \left( {2x + 1} \right)$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$2 x 3 -2x+2 2 x 3 -2x+2$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <paragraph>For the following exercises, use synthetic division to determine whether the first expression is a factor of the second. If it is, indicate the factorization.</paragraph>
    <exercise number="38" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$x - 2, 4x^{3} - 3x^{2} - 8x + 4$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="39" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$x - 2, 3x^{4} - 6x^{3} - 5x + 10$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>Yes $$( x-2 )(3 x 3 -5) ( x-2 )(3 x 3 -5)$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="40" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$x + 3, - 4x^{3} + 5x^{2} + 8$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="41" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$x - 2, 4x^{4} - 15x^{2} - 4$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>Yes $$( x-2 )(4 x 3 +8 x 2 +x+2) ( x-2 )(4 x 3 +8 x 2 +x+2)$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="42" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$x - \frac{1}{2}, 2x^{4} - x^{3} + 2x - 1$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="43" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$x + \frac{1}{3}, 3x^{4} + x^{3} - 3x + 1$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>No</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <heading level="1">Graphical</heading>
    <paragraph>For the following exercises, use the graph of the third-degree polynomial and one factor to write the factored form of the polynomial suggested by the graph. The leading coefficient is one.</paragraph>
    <exercise number="44" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>Factor is $$x^{2} - x + 3$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="45" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>Factor is $$(x^{2} + 2x + 4)$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$(x-1)( x 2 +2x+4) (x-1)( x 2 +2x+4)$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="46" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>Factor is $$x^{2} + 2x + 5$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="47" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>Factor is $$x^{2} + x + 1$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$(x-5)( x 2 +x+1) (x-5)( x 2 +x+1)$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="48" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>Factor is $$x^{2} + 2x + 2$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <paragraph>For the following exercises, use synthetic division to find the quotient and remainder.</paragraph>
    <exercise number="49" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\frac{4x^{3} - 33}{x - 2}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$Quotient:4 x 2 +8x+16,remainder:-1 Quotient:4 x 2 +8x+16,remainder:-1$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="50" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\frac{2x^{3} + 25}{x + 3}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="51" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\frac{3x^{3} + 2x - 5}{x - 1}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$Quotient:3 x 2 +3x+5,remainder:0 Quotient:3 x 2 +3x+5,remainder:0$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="52" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\frac{- 4x^{3} - x^{2} - 12}{x + 4}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="53" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\frac{x^{4} - 22}{x + 2}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$Quotient: x 3 -2 x 2 +4x-8,remainder:-6 Quotient: x 3 -2 x 2 +4x-8,remainder:-6$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <heading level="1">Technology</heading>
    <paragraph>For the following exercises, use a calculator with CAS to answer the questions.</paragraph>
    <exercise number="54" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>Consider $$\frac{x^{k} - 1}{x - 1}$$ with $$k = 1, 2, 3.$$ What do you expect the result to be if $$k = 4?$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="55" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>Consider $$\frac{x^{k} + 1}{x + 1}$$ for $$k = 1, 3, 5.$$ What do you expect the result to be if $$k = 7?$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$x 6 - x 5 + x 4 - x 3 + x 2 -x+1 x 6 - x 5 + x 4 - x 3 + x 2 -x+1$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="56" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>Consider $$\frac{x^{4} - k^{4}}{x - k}$$ for $$k = 1, 2, 3.$$ What do you expect the result to be if $$k = 4?$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="57" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>Consider $$\frac{x^{k}}{x + 1}$$ with $$k = 1, 2, 3.$$ What do you expect the result to be if $$k = 4?$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$x 3 - x 2 +x-1+ 1 x+1 x 3 - x 2 +x-1+ 1 x+1$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="58" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>Consider $$\frac{x^{k}}{x - 1}$$ with $$k = 1, 2, 3.$$ What do you expect the result to be if $$k = 4?$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <heading level="1">Extensions</heading>
    <paragraph>For the following exercises, use synthetic division to determine the quotient involving a complex number.</paragraph>
    <exercise number="59" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\frac{x + 1}{x - i}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$1+ 1+i x-i 1+ 1+i x-i$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="60" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\frac{x^{2} + 1}{x - i}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="61" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\frac{x + 1}{x + i}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$1+ 1-i x+i 1+ 1-i x+i$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="62" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\frac{x^{2} + 1}{x + i}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="63" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\frac{x^{3} + 1}{x - i}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$x 2 +ix-1+ 1-i x-i x 2 +ix-1+ 1-i x-i$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <heading level="1">Real-World Applications</heading>
    <paragraph>For the following exercises, use the given length and area of a rectangle to express the width algebraically.</paragraph>
    <exercise number="64" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>Length is $$x + 5,$$ area is $$2x^{2} + 9x - 5.$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="65" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>Length is $$2x + 5,$$ area is $$4x^{3} + 10x^{2} + 6x + 15$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$2 x 2 +3 2 x 2 +3$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="66" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>Length is $$3x-4,$$ area is $$6x^{4} - 8x^{3} + 9x^{2} - 9x - 4$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <paragraph>For the following exercises, use the given volume of a box and its length and width to express the height of the box algebraically.</paragraph>
    <exercise number="67" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>Volume is $$12x^{3} + 20x^{2} - 21x - 36,$$ length is $$2x + 3,$$ width is $$3x - 4.$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$2x+3 2x+3$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="68" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>Volume is $$18x^{3} - 21x^{2} - 40x + 48,$$ length is $$3x-4,$$ width is $$3x-4.$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="69" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>Volume is $$10x^{3} + 27x^{2} + 2x - 24,$$ length is $$5x-4,$$ width is $$2x + 3.$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$x+2 x+2$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="70" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>Volume is $$10x^{3} + 30x^{2} - 8x - 24,$$ length is $$2,$$ width is $$x + 3.$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <paragraph>For the following exercises, use the given volume and radius of a cylinder to express the height of the cylinder algebraically.</paragraph>
    <exercise number="71" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>Volume is $$\pi\left( 25x^{3} - 65x^{2} - 29x - 3 \right),$$ radius is $$5x + 1.$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$x-3 x-3$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="72" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>Volume is $$\pi\left( 4x^{3} + 12x^{2} - 15x - 50 \right),$$ radius is $$2x + 5.$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="73" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>Volume is $$\pi\left( 3x^{4} + 24x^{3} + 46x^{2} - 16x - 32 \right),$$ radius is $$x + 4.$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$3 x 2 -2 3 x 2 -2$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
  </exercises>
</section>
